<title>USA: Central Newspapers May revenues up.</title>
<headline>Central Newspapers May revenues up.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Newspapers Inc said Thursday revenues for the four-week period ended May 25 rose 14 percent versus the comparable period last year.</p>
<p>Revenues for the month were $56.35 milllion, up from $49.45 million.</p>
<p>Year to date, revenues rose 16.2 percent to $283.38 million from $243.77 million.</p>
<p>Full run-of-press advertising linage rose 8.5 percent for the month and 15.3 percent year to date.</p>
<p>Central Newspapers is a media company publishing daily, Sunday and weekly newspapers.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
